# Milestone: M1
# Covers: block comments are NON-NESTING — the first */ closes the comment
#         regardless of intervening /* sequences.  Matches C semantics.
# Audit:   LEX-034 (no fixture or doc on this previously).

# --- the first */ closes the outer comment; everything after the */ is code
/* outer /* inner */ 42
[00000001] 42

# --- a tail */ outside the comment is just a syntax error in the surrounding
# expression; what matters here is that the lexer treats the FIRST */ as the
# closing delimiter — verified above.  Re-enter a clean expression to confirm
# the lexer state is sane after the prior fixture line.
1 + 2
[00000002] 3
